->OS detected as well

Step B: Web server analysis (**Nikto**) -> Manual PT
kali$ nikto -h http://10.0.2.5
->apache outdated = high risk
->wordpress indicators found (content disclosure, cms) = medium risk 
->security headers missing (x-frame options not set, clickjacking; x-content-type-options missing, mime sniffing attack) = medium risk
=>The server is hosting a potentially vulnerable CMS (Drupal/WordPress), is missing several basic HTTP security headers, and runs outdated software versions - all of which contribute to a weak attack surface. Additionally, the presence of Webmin interface (MiniServ) suggestsa potential vector for remote code execution (RCE).




